## 229. Majority Element II

## Approach

- Since we need elements appearing more than n/3 times, there can be at most two majority elements.
- Maintain two candidates and two voting counts.
- Traverse the array and use the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm to find the two possible candidates.
- If the current number matches candidate1, increase count1.
- Else if it matches candidate2, increase count2.
- If count1 is 0, make the current number candidate1.
- Else if count2 is 0, make the current number candidate2.
- Otherwise, decrease both counts because the current number is different from both candidates.
- After finding the two possible candidates, traverse the array again to count their actual occurrences.
- If a candidate appears more than n/3 times, add it to the result list.

## Complexity

- Time: O(n)
- Space: O(1)

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> majorityElement(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int candidate1 = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int candidate2 = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
        int count1 = 0;
        int count2 = 0;
        int actualCount1 = 0;
        int actualCount2 = 0;

        ArrayList<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int num : nums) {
            if (num == candidate1) {
                count1++;
            } else if (num == candidate2) {
                count2++;
            } else if (count1 == 0) {
                candidate1 = num;
                count1 = 1;
            } else if (count2 == 0) {
                candidate2 = num;
                count2 = 1;
            } else {
                count1--;
                count2--;
            }
        }
        
        // For actual count of candidates
        for (int num : nums) {
            if (num == candidate1)
                actualCount1++;
            if (num == candidate2)
                actualCount2++;
        }
        if (actualCount1 > (n / 3)) {
            result.add(candidate1);
        }
        if (actualCount2 > (n / 3)) {
            result.add(candidate2);
        }
        return result;
    }
}
